      "side": 1,
      "message": "Overall, I\u0027d recommend avoid using conversion functions with different names. Prefer something like `ndk2cpp` with overloads.\n\nE.g. then you can do things like this:\n\n\n```\ntemplate \u003ctypename NDK, typename CPP\u003e\nstd::optional\u003cNDK\u003e ndk2cpp(const std::optional\u003cCPP\u003e\u0026 cpp) {\n    if (cpp \u003d\u003d std::nullopt) return std::nullopt;\n    return ndk2cpp(cpp.get());\n}\n```\n\nThen, that logic only has to be written once. Same with other functions - take advantage of algebraic type system.",
      "revId": "b2743395a9e08c4302247135738de557b6e83e79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
